		{"id":"100bf9b9b82992e4","type":"text","text":"Money\n--- \n### Net Cafe\nLowk the only realworld net cafe in Kyoto that offered a 1 week plan was CocoNe net cafe. 23,990 for the mat-type room \n![[Pasted image 20260221005250.png]]\nHer first client probably gave her like 25k lowk (truly a miracle cure)\n### Apartment\n18 sq meters and 18k per month\n\nhttps://rentola.com/listings/p50f00d\n\nI think we can haggle with the price though, and it doesn't have to be 100% accurate to real japan.\n\nThough tbh 18k per month is doable considering the nature of the pay. The downpayment is just the issue (maybe Shinki haggles it down to 45k because she's just that business oriented)","x":-1360,"y":-1360,"width":490,"height":560},
		{"id":"258601a040bb942c","type":"text","text":"Should be paid on avg like 30k per successful thing by the end of it.","x":-1280,"y":-742,"width":250,"height":202},
		{"id":"ca026a6c5d65d409","type":"text","text":"# Brainstorming\n---\n## Game beats:\n\n### Beginning:\n--- \n* Game starts in a Rakugo Hall. Shinigami kun is telling the story, as a jellyfish. Disclaimer that everyone is a jellyfish before he becomes his Gijinka form.\n\t* Do a Rakugo bit before bowing and moving onto the next scene\n\t\n* (March 31st) Meet Shinki, a jellyfish girl recently kicked out of her house for being framed for embezzlement. She's at her lowest point, but the closer she's pushed to death the more determined she is to make money\n* Meet Shinigami kun, who wants to torment her but is fascinated by her business proposal, and agrees. Possesses Shinki.\n\n* Start quack doctor scheme (Shinki: \"If it works, is it really a scam?\")\n\t* Tutorial for quack doctor scheme. Will be used in the management sim aspect\n\t* You go into the house, see the patient in their futon. \n\t* Shinigami kun will be at the foot of the bed (ik it might not be accurate to the story but for game reasons I really want it to work like this.)\n\n### Management Sim part\n--- \n* Rounds span a week. Each round has x turns.\n    *  General Round things:\n    \t* Beginning of Round: Advertise, Customize office, Go Shopping\n        \t* Certain items make the game easier, boost your chances of feet shinigami, or are just requests from Shinigami kun\n\t        \t* Money Omamori: 500 yen\n        * Middle of Round: Go to different places, heal or refuse.\n        * End of Round: Hang out with Shinigami kun (Affection meter maybe? Or satisfaction meter ig. This is required or else he will leave. Maybe). Some events require money\n        * You can only choose up to 5 clients per round. You can choose them from a pool of 10 though\n\t        * Maybe there's an item that lets you choose up to 7 per round?\n    * Nozaki Family are a forced event and will come depending on your money threshold during a round, or will come when you buy a certain item\n* Hiue Family\n\t* Fatal disease in the balls. I'm joking that it's caused by Shinigami kun but he did really want it to happen.\n    * Shinigami kun wants to go only so he can be the one to do his brother in. \n    * Shinki goes, but then decides to work with Jirou and tricks Shinigami kun- who gets driven away.\n\t    * Idk, maybe like \n    * She gets thanked, etc etc, and then when she leaves the building she sees Shinigami kun waiting outside\n    * Gets dragged out to the underworld and sees the candles. See [[The Shinigami that is also a Jellyfish#Endings (most result in you becoming a shinigami)|Endings]]\n- List of rounds: \n\t- Round 1: \n\t\t- Right after Shinki finishes the tutorial. She doesn't have enough money for an apartment so she lives in a net cafe for the time being  \n\t\t- Lowk this is a good time for a general game tutorial since there isn't much to do other than make money (general idea of how the menus work)\n- Numbers by round\n\n| Round |     | Payment* | Forced Jellyfish Encounters       | Available Events                                                              | Special Items to Buy |\n| ----- | --- | -------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| 1     |     | 5-10k    | N/A                               | <br>- Read Manga<br>- Conbini run<br>- Surf the web<br>- Play in the park<br> |                      |\n| 2     |     | 10-15k   |                                   |                                                                               | - Apartment<br>      |\n| 3     |     | 10-17k   |                                   |                                                                               | Nozakike charm       |\n| 4     |     | 15-20k   | Nozakike (if you haven't already) |                                                                               |                      |\n| 5     |     | 15-25k   | Jirou                             |                                                                               |                      |\n*\\*Anything above the cap will be a guaranteed fail*\n\n### Endings (most result in you dying):\n* **Love ending**: Maybe kinda yandere? Not sure. \n\t* If you do a certain amount of events. Shinki becomes his raison d'ete, but after the betrayal he decides that he'll just keep her here. Forever.\n* **Candle endings**: Have the candle scene. Hold the candle with the mouse and wait until its lit fully. \n\t* If the player moves the candle before it's //fully// lit, she will die. Shinigami kun will talk while this happens so if the player moves mouse to move along with his dialogue, they die (\"Haha. You think you could light anything with those shakey hands?\"). You just have to hold still and let him talk. (God. This is peak role embodiment tho, You have to ignore him)\n\t\t* Note: Maybe have the candle shake a little by itself and you have to fangangle against it? I like that better lowk\n\t\t* The shinigami will still talk but if you don't fanangle against Shinki's hands while you read then you die\n    * If player lights the candle\n    \t* 1% chance she sneezes and blows it out (get fucked lol) (rolls each time the scene is loaded for the completionists)\n        * Otherwise, Shinigami kun just claps and disappears- ending the interaction and friendship coldly.\n        * Then Shinki goes home as if nothing ever happend...\n        \t* Actually, when Shinki goes to sleep, she sees him by the head of her futon. \"Shit\"\n            * If you didn't buy ofuda (very hard, you need to make a lot of money and fight Shinki on the menuing), the game ends there. Otherwise, you slap the ofuda on him and uh, it gives you enough time to escape. \n            * The win is empty though, and you're back to square one. Now with a shinigami on your heels. Escape the country\n\n\nNotes:\nShinigami kun\n* Prefers his new life as a Shinigami. (Only rly lived in fear as Shirou, though he won't admit that to Shinki)\n* Prized possession is the letter Saburou wrote to him before death. He doesn't have it anymore, but he has at least half of it memorized.\n* Can eat, but only when offered food through people who have a connection with him (can't have him be too ghost-ly now. He must still be bound by the rules of death)\n\t* Could be a good view into what dead people are like in Ite, since we have two ghosts. Nozaki-chan would prolly be able to bend the rules thanks to her lineage tho\n\nShinigami Lore\n* Not psychopomps (?), makes the candle thing kinda obselete\n\t* Though Shinigami nowadays are understood to be grim reapers\n* Cave of candles \n\t* Tbh this part isn't particularly Japanese, since it was imported from a western story. Struggling to incorporate it into the story.\n","x":-760,"y":-1860,"width":1220,"height":2600}
	],
